# Stage 8A: strict build-context exclusions. The Dockerfile's runtime
# stage copies application source by EXPLICIT path (never `COPY . .`), so
# this file's main effect is (a) keeping the context small/fast to send to
# the daemon and (b) a defense-in-depth backstop against anything an
# explicit COPY path might otherwise pick up (nested caches, stray
# secrets, the reference-corpus directory's non-allowlisted contents).
#
# IMPORTANT: every exclusion below that targets a bare filename or a
# top-level directory is duplicated with a `**/` prefix. A bare pattern
# like `__pycache__/` only matches at the root of the build context, NOT
# inside nested package directories (app/, db/, handlers/, rag/,
# scripts/, services/, utils/, web/, alembic/, ...) — omitting the `**/`
# form is exactly what previously let nested __pycache__/*.pyc into the
# final image. Keep both forms when adding new rules here.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT add a blanket `data/documents/*` negation change —
# only the four exact reference-corpus filenames below may be
# re-included; any other file dropped into data/documents/ (including
# uploads/) must stay excluded. See rag/constants.BUILTIN_REFERENCE_FILES
# for the source of truth these four names are copied from.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# Local AI tool/runtime metadata (session state, lock files, PIDs,
# timestamps) — never a build input, must never reach the daemon.
.claude/
**/.claude/

# Environment / secrets — never baked into the image; real values are
# injected at container-run time via the orchestrator's own env/secret
# mechanism instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# npm / pip publish credentials
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.pypirc
**/.pypirc

# Private keys, certificate bundles, SSH material
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
*.crt
**/*.crt
*.cer
**/*.cer
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
**/id_ed25519*
.ssh/
**/.ssh/

# Credential / secret files and directories
*credentials*
**/*credentials*
*.secret
**/*.secret
secrets/
**/secrets/

# Python virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/env/
**/ENV/

# Python caches / test caches (recursive — see IMPORTANT note above)
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*$py.class
**/*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.coverage
**/.coverage
.coverage.*
**/.coverage.*
htmlcov/
**/htmlcov/

# Test suite — dev-only, not part of the production runtime image.
tests/
requirements-dev.txt
pytest.ini

# Frontend: dependencies are installed fresh inside the builder stage
# (`npm ci`), and any locally-built dist/ must never shadow a real build.
frontend/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
**/npm-debug.log*

# Logs / log artifacts
*.log
**/*.log
bot.log
**/bot.log

# Local-only application data — never shipped inside the image.
# data/qdrant and data/documents/uploads are recreated empty inside the
# image and owned by the non-root runtime user instead (see Dockerfile);
# the other two are legacy/generated local artifacts.
data/qdrant/
**/data/qdrant/
data/chroma_db/
data/generated_images/
data/embeddings.db

# Reference corpus allowlist: only the four committed Markdown files
# rag/constants.BUILTIN_REFERENCE_FILES enumerates may enter the image.
# This blanket-excludes everything else directly under data/documents/
# (including uploads/, .gitkeep, and any ignored/private local file that
# might be dropped there) and re-includes only those four by exact name.
data/documents/*
!data/documents/python-fundamentals.md
!data/documents/functions-classes-errors.md
!data/documents/testing-debugging.md
!data/documents/async-python-and-apis.md

# IDE / OS / editor cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Repository docs not needed at runtime
README.md
docs/
